  "rules": [
    "Capacity floors are reservation targets, not claims about Generation 10 content counts.",
    "A table family gets a concrete stride/encoding only after its Gen III consumers and modern requirements are audited.",
    "Expanded-profile code must use directory metadata and logical counts instead of historical fixed-end constants.",
    "Existing Gen III Unown compatibility encoding must be mapped explicitly before species IDs are appended.",
    "Form-change runtime remains inactive until explicitly resumed.",
